# MystoraX doctrine (always on)

- Prefer Conductor `POST /v1/goal` / `mystorax_submit_goal` over bridges or CLIs.
- Discover: routing guide → surfaces → submit goal. Bootstrap: `GET /v1/hosts/manifest`.
- Files: ChatGPT or Perplexity only. Gemini text-only.
- Hands: thin apply/download/check — `gemini → copilot → codex → cursor-agent → claude`.
- Multi-step work stays in ONE author session (50–200+ steps). Escalate before switch.
- Science auto-resume stops at EVIDENCE. Never auto-CERTIFY.
- HARD refuse: Computer / ASI / agentic_research / Spark / local LLM / agy execute.
- No secrets in git. No invented bridge URLs. No front owns doctrine.
